//? Title: Subset sum: exact half sums and actual witness lookups
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Meet in the middle replaces full-subset enumeration with two exponential half
spaces. Actual widened sums, sort comparisons and lookup probes retain the
original signed examples while avoiding overflow in sums and target differences.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Split n keys at floor(n/2). Enumerate every right-half mask, sort its sums, then
enumerate left masks and binary-search target-left_sum. Any full witness
decomposes into exactly such a pair. Directly scanning each mask costs
O(n*2^ceil(n/2)); sorting and repeated binary searches add their logarithmic
factors. The original2^n versus2^(n/2) curves compare search-space sizes, not
measured runtime speedups. Negative values and the empty subset are valid.
Private signed128 arithmetic is exact for at most62 signed64 keys and one
signed64 target difference.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/subset_sum_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::subset_sum_trace({3, -2, 5}, 1);
    std::print("| actual right mask | exact sum |\n| ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.right)
        std::print("| {} | {} |\n", s.mask, s.sum);
    std::print("\n| actual left mask | exact left sum | needed | matched | right mask |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.probes)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.left_mask, s.left_sum,
                   s.needed, s.matched, s.right_mask);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual keys3,-2,5; target1");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} right masks enumerated",
                                     r.right_subsets));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual witness indices {}",
                                     r.result.indices));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/subset_sum_tiny.svg");
}
```
