> API and interpretation

Complete half-subset geometry is checked before allocation; intrinsic n<=62
protects masks and exact accumulator capacity. Default policies permit at
most2million right masks. Sorting equal sums does not promise a particular tied
right witness. The API returns one actual subset rather than all witnesses, and
the report labels theoretical search-space ratios as references.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Horowitz and Sahni, Computing Partitions with Applications to the Knapsack
  Problem, JACM21 (1974),277-292

